WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.705
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Sunday, November twenty second.

2
00:00:04.705 --> 00:00:12.369
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.369 --> 00:00:14.933
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:30.155
Today: a new Iranian attack on Bahrain, cartel violence in Mexico's Sinaloa state after a major arrest, a drone strike on a Russian cargo ship in the Gulf of Finland, and a quadcopter attack on a peace meeting in northwest Pakistan.

5
00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:30.987
We start in Bahrain.

6
00:00:30.987 --> 00:00:37.307
Reuters reports Bahrain says an Iranian attack hit an industrial facility as its air defenses intercepted attacks.

7
00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:44.892
Separately, Reuters reports the United States denied an Iranian account that a missile damaged a U.S.

8
00:00:44.892 --> 00:00:45.766
F-16 over the Gulf.

9
00:00:45.766 --> 00:00:46.716
Next, Mexico.

10
00:00:46.716 --> 00:00:49.053
The State Department says the U.S.

11
00:00:49.053 --> 00:01:01.417
Consulate General in Hermosillo is monitoring reports of security operations, armed clashes, road blockades and vehicle fires overnight in Ahome, Guamúchil, Guasave and Navolato in Sinaloa state, following the arrest of Fausto Isidro Meza Flores.

12
00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:11.812
Crisis Group says the cartel leader, known as El Chapo Isidro, was captured by Mexican authorities in Guasave on Friday night, November twentieth.

13
00:01:11.812 --> 00:01:13.846
Turning to the Baltic.

14
00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:25.208
The Institute for the Study of War says two Ukrainian drones struck the Russian cargo ship Sparta Two, which has supported Russian military logistics, in the Gulf of Finland.

15
00:01:25.208 --> 00:01:33.584
Reuters reports Finland says the ship is on fire in its waters, that Finland has tightened security, and that the ship was still burning early today.

16
00:01:33.584 --> 00:01:45.259
And in Pakistan, Tribal News Network reports a quadcopter attack on a jirga, or council of elders, in Bannu, in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province, injured ten people, including children, with several in critical condition.

17
00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:47.304
Global Decipher reports at least twenty were injured.

18
00:01:47.304 --> 00:01:50.300
Accounts differ on who carried out the attack.

19
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:55.069
Now a few quick notes by region.

20
00:01:55.069 --> 00:02:12.238
In the Middle East, the Institute for the Study of War says the Houthis are reportedly reinforcing positions and military capabilities along the Bab el Mandeb Strait, citing unnamed military and local sources, and assesses that Saudi Arabia is carrying out airstrikes on Houthi energy infrastructure.

21
00:02:12.238 --> 00:02:22.004
In Iran, Radio Free Europe Radio Liberty reports the government said it will ration electricity, days after it began managing bread purchases because of shortages.

22
00:02:22.004 --> 00:02:30.359
In Africa, on Thursday night, November nineteenth, gunmen attacked the edge of Nangade town in Mozambique's Cabo Delgado province.

23
00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:33.190
Zitamar News reports six people were killed.

24
00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:39.569
The terrorism monitor TRAC says Christians were targeted and attributes the attack to Islamic State Mozambique.

25
00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:56.727
In Europe, the Institute for the Study of War says Ukraine's president proposed temporary local ceasefires to evacuate civilians from fifteen settlements along the Dnipro River in occupied Kherson and Zaporizhzhia regions, and that Russian forces recently advanced in several areas of eastern Ukraine.

26
00:02:56.727 --> 00:03:07.286
In the Americas, InSight Crime reports violence is rising in a Venezuelan mining zone disputed by the E L N and the Second Marquetalia, displacing Indigenous communities.

27
00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:08.742
That's today's brief.

28
00:03:08.742 --> 00:03:16.996
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

29
00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:25.308
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

30
00:03:25.308 --> 00:03:27.460
This brief is digitally narrated.

31
00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.406
Questions?

32
00:03:28.406 --> 00:03:31.906
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

33
00:03:31.906 --> 00:03:34.154
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
